WEBVTT

00:02.438 --> 00:04.356
Water.

00:04.565 --> 00:06.275
Earth.

00:06.567 --> 00:08.360
Fire.

00:08.820 --> 00:10.612
Air.

00:10.822 --> 00:14.408
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.326 --> 00:18.370
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.580 --> 00:21.790
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:21.874 --> 00:23.458
could stop them.

00:23.793 --> 00:26.753
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

00:27.213 --> 00:31.008
100 years passed, and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.301 --> 00:32.884
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.094 --> 00:35.137
And although his
airbending skills are great,

00:35.221 --> 00:37.681
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.807 --> 00:38.849
Unh!

00:38.933 --> 00:42.019
But I believe Aang can save the world.

01:15.303 --> 01:16.845
We need you, Aang.

01:17.221 --> 01:19.014
I need you, too.

01:24.979 --> 01:27.064
Be careful, guys!

01:27.148 --> 01:28.315
Guys?

01:29.692 --> 01:30.859
Gyatso?

01:30.943 --> 01:32.611
Why did you disappear?

01:33.237 --> 01:34.738
I didn't mean to.

01:40.995 --> 01:43.080
We need you, Aang.

01:48.336 --> 01:50.587
We need you, Aang.
We need you.

01:51.130 --> 01:53.715
We need you, Aang. We need you.

01:55.885 --> 01:57.636
What's going on?

01:57.720 --> 01:58.970
Did we get captured again?

01:59.263 --> 02:01.431
It's nothing. I just had a bad dream.

02:01.557 --> 02:02.766
Go back to sleep.

02:02.850 --> 02:03.934
You don't have to tell me twice.

02:04.644 --> 02:05.894
Are you all right, Aang?

02:05.978 --> 02:07.062
I'm okay.

02:07.271 --> 02:09.106
You seem to be having
a lot of nightmares lately.

02:09.190 --> 02:10.982
You want to tell me about it?

02:11.067 --> 02:12.818
I think I just need some rest.

02:12.902 --> 02:15.529
You guys want to hear about my dream?

02:16.114 --> 02:19.074
That's okay. I didn't want
to talk about it anyway.

02:24.163 --> 02:25.497
Look at those clear skies, buddy.

02:25.998 --> 02:27.582
Should be some smooth flying.

02:29.627 --> 02:32.629
Well, we'd better
smoothly fly ourselves to a market,

02:32.713 --> 02:33.922
because we're out of food.

02:34.132 --> 02:36.174
Guys, wait. This was in my dream.

02:36.259 --> 02:37.592
We shouldn't go to the market.

02:37.677 --> 02:38.718
What happened in your dream?

02:39.137 --> 02:40.804
Food eats people!

02:41.889 --> 02:44.266
Also, Momo could talk.

02:44.475 --> 02:46.309
You said some very unkind things.

02:53.651 --> 02:55.527
There is a storm coming.

02:55.736 --> 02:56.903
A big one.

02:57.113 --> 02:58.530
You're out of your mind, uncle.

02:58.614 --> 03:00.740
The weather is perfect.
There's not a cloud in sight.

03:01.534 --> 03:04.327
A storm is approaching from the north.

03:04.704 --> 03:08.498
I suggest we alter our course
and head southwest.

03:08.708 --> 03:10.417
We know the Avatar
is traveling northward,

03:10.501 --> 03:12.085
so we will do the same.

03:12.503 --> 03:15.297
Prince Zuko,
consider the safety of the crew.

03:15.506 --> 03:17.757
The safety of the crew doesn't matter.

03:21.179 --> 03:24.181
Finding the Avatar
is far more important

03:24.265 --> 03:26.224
than any individual's safety.

03:30.188 --> 03:33.648
He doesn't mean that.
He's just all worked up.

03:36.986 --> 03:39.488
It's good.
It's perfect, I'm telling you.

03:41.491 --> 03:43.700
I don't know if I like
the sound of that swishing.

03:43.910 --> 03:45.327
Swishing means it's ripe.

03:45.536 --> 03:49.080
It's the ripe juices
swishing around?

03:49.290 --> 03:50.582
I think it's true, Katara.

03:50.666 --> 03:51.875
Swishing means it's ripe.

03:52.418 --> 03:54.294
I just realized
we're out of money, anyway.

03:55.505 --> 03:57.297
Aww...

04:00.885 --> 04:02.802
Out of food and out of money.

04:02.887 --> 04:04.304
Now what are we supposed to do?

04:04.514 --> 04:06.264
You could get a job, smart guy.

04:06.474 --> 04:07.724
We shouldn't go out there.

04:07.808 --> 04:09.768
Please! The fish can wait.

04:09.852 --> 04:11.686
There's going to be a terrible storm.

04:11.896 --> 04:14.356
Aw, you're crazy. It's a nice day.

04:14.440 --> 04:16.483
No clouds, no wind, no nothing,

04:16.692 --> 04:18.485
so quit your nagging, woman.

04:18.694 --> 04:21.404
Maybe we should find some shelter.

04:21.614 --> 04:23.782
Are you kidding? Shelter from what?

04:23.991 --> 04:26.409
My joints say
there's going to be a storm,

04:26.494 --> 04:27.869
a bad one.

04:28.204 --> 04:30.914
Well, it's your joints
against my brain.

04:31.123 --> 04:33.625
Then I hope your brain can find
someone else to haul that fish,

04:33.709 --> 04:34.793
'cause I ain't coming!

04:35.002 --> 04:36.753
Then I'll find a new fish hauler,

04:36.837 --> 04:38.296
and pay him double what you get.

04:38.548 --> 04:39.548
How do you like that?

04:39.632 --> 04:40.632
I'll go.

04:40.716 --> 04:41.967
You're hired.

04:43.261 --> 04:45.220
What? You said get a job.

04:45.429 --> 04:46.721
And he's paying double.

04:46.889 --> 04:49.015
Double? Who told you that nonsense?

04:55.648 --> 04:59.067
Looks like your uncle was right
about the storm after all.

04:59.151 --> 05:00.277
Lucky guess.

05:00.361 --> 05:02.612
Lieutenant,
you'd better learn some respect,

05:03.281 --> 05:05.907
or I will teach it to you.

05:06.284 --> 05:08.577
What do you know about respect?

05:10.288 --> 05:12.789
The way you talk
to everyone around here,

05:12.999 --> 05:15.667
from your hard-working crew
to your esteemed uncle,

05:15.876 --> 05:18.962
shows you know nothing about respect.

05:19.171 --> 05:21.840
You don't care about
anyone but yourself.

05:22.049 --> 05:26.052
Then again, what should I expect
from a spoiled prince?

05:30.057 --> 05:31.266
Easy now.

05:34.770 --> 05:36.021
Enough!

05:36.480 --> 05:40.358
We're all a bit tired
from being at sea so long.

05:40.943 --> 05:43.069
I'm sure after a bowl of noodles,

05:43.279 --> 05:46.156
everyone will feel much better.

05:48.951 --> 05:51.536
I don't need your help
keeping order on my ship.

06:00.129 --> 06:02.756
Sokka, maybe this isn't
such a good idea.

06:02.840 --> 06:04.007
Look at the sky.

06:04.091 --> 06:05.634
I said I was gonna do this job.

06:05.718 --> 06:07.844
I can't back out just because
of some bad weather.

06:08.888 --> 06:11.264
The boy with the tattoos
has some sense.

06:11.349 --> 06:12.432
You should listen to him.

06:12.642 --> 06:14.768
Boy with tattoos?

06:14.977 --> 06:16.978
Airbender tattoos.

06:17.313 --> 06:20.023
Well, I'll be a hog monkey's uncle.

06:20.107 --> 06:21.524
You're the Avatar, ain't you?

06:21.817 --> 06:22.901
That's right.

06:23.152 --> 06:24.861
Well, don't be so smiley about it.

06:26.238 --> 06:28.740
The Avatar disappeared
for a hundred years!

06:28.991 --> 06:30.867
You turned your back on the world.

06:31.077 --> 06:32.744
Don't yell at him!

06:32.828 --> 06:34.913
Aang would never
turn his back on anyone.

06:35.164 --> 06:37.123
He wouldn't?

06:37.416 --> 06:39.042
Then I guess I must have imagined

06:39.126 --> 06:42.253
the last hundred years
of war and suffering.

06:42.880 --> 06:44.923
Aang is the bravest person I know.

06:45.132 --> 06:46.925
He has done nothing but help people,

06:47.009 --> 06:49.260
and save lives since I met him.

06:49.470 --> 06:51.930
It's not his fault he disappeared,
right, Aang?

06:52.139 --> 06:53.682
Aang, what's wrong?

06:56.852 --> 06:58.895
That's right! Keep flying!

06:59.105 --> 07:00.689
You're a horrible old man!

07:05.111 --> 07:06.986
Appa, yip yip!

07:08.239 --> 07:10.407
Hey! They left
without saying good-bye.

07:10.616 --> 07:12.575
Your friends ain't too polite,
are they?

07:12.868 --> 07:14.703
I know. This one time, I was--

07:14.787 --> 07:16.705
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Get below deck.

07:37.143 --> 07:38.768
I'm sorry for running away.

07:38.853 --> 07:41.521
It's okay. That fisherman
was way out of line.

07:42.231 --> 07:44.065
Actually, he wasn't.

07:44.275 --> 07:46.651
What do you mean?

07:46.861 --> 07:48.528
I don't want to talk about it.

07:48.738 --> 07:51.281
It has to do with your dream,
doesn't it?

07:51.490 --> 07:52.907
Talk to me.

07:53.117 --> 07:55.410
Well, it's kind of a long story.

08:01.417 --> 08:03.710
I'm gonna try to get
a little fire going.

08:07.006 --> 08:09.924
I'll never forget the day
the monks told me I was the Avatar.

08:12.219 --> 08:15.221
I was playing with some other kids
just outside the south wall.

08:15.473 --> 08:17.891
I was trying to teach them
how to do the air scooter.

08:18.184 --> 08:21.394
First you form a ball.
Then you've got to get on quick.

08:23.189 --> 08:24.397
Ha ha ha!

08:24.607 --> 08:26.608
Yeah! Ha ha ha!

08:26.692 --> 08:28.276
Whoo-hoo! Yeah!

08:28.778 --> 08:31.237
Okay, here goes.

08:31.447 --> 08:32.447
Quick. Get on.

08:32.531 --> 08:34.991
Whoa. Whoa...

08:37.077 --> 08:39.162
You kind of have to balance on it
like it's a top.

08:39.371 --> 08:41.080
Man, that's hard.

08:41.290 --> 08:42.707
Where did you learn that trick, Aang?

08:42.875 --> 08:44.000
I made it up.

08:44.084 --> 08:45.627
Wow!

08:45.836 --> 08:47.796
Aang, come with us.

08:48.005 --> 08:49.798
We need to speak with you.

08:57.139 --> 08:58.723
How do you know it's me?

08:58.808 --> 09:02.143
We have known you were
the Avatar for some time.

09:02.728 --> 09:04.145
Do you remember these?

09:08.901 --> 09:11.653
Those were some of my favorite toys
when I was little.

09:11.862 --> 09:14.781
You chose them
from among thousands of toys, Aang.

09:15.157 --> 09:18.993
The toys you picked
were the four Avatar relics.

09:19.286 --> 09:22.163
These items belonged to Avatars past.

09:22.373 --> 09:24.415
Your own past lives.

09:24.500 --> 09:26.584
I just chose them
because they seemed fun.

09:27.253 --> 09:29.796
You chose them
because they were familiar.

09:30.214 --> 09:34.634
Normally, we would have told you
of your identity when you turned 16.

09:35.010 --> 09:37.470
But there are troubling signs.

09:37.680 --> 09:40.515
Storm clouds are gathering.

09:40.933 --> 09:44.435
I fear that war may be upon us,
young Avatar.

09:44.645 --> 09:46.145
We need you, Aang.

09:53.988 --> 09:55.905
I'm sick of taking his orders,

09:56.115 --> 09:58.032
and I'm tired of chasing his Avatar.

09:58.242 --> 10:00.535
I mean, who does Zuko think he is?

10:00.744 --> 10:02.495
Do you really want to know?

10:02.705 --> 10:04.497
General Iroh, we were just--

10:04.582 --> 10:06.124
It's okay.

10:06.333 --> 10:07.625
May I join you?

10:07.710 --> 10:08.751
Of course, sir.

10:12.631 --> 10:14.299
Try to understand,

10:14.550 --> 10:16.926
my nephew is a complicated young man.

10:17.177 --> 10:19.012
He has been through much.

10:25.311 --> 10:26.519
Let me in!

10:26.604 --> 10:28.396
Prince Zuko, what's wrong?

10:28.606 --> 10:30.023
I want to go into the war chamber,

10:30.107 --> 10:31.858
but the guard won't let me pass.

10:31.942 --> 10:34.444
You're not missing anything. Trust me.

10:34.570 --> 10:37.447
These meetings are dreadfully boring.

10:37.740 --> 10:39.741
If I'm going to rule
this nation one day,

10:39.825 --> 10:42.160
don't you think I need
to start learning as much as I can?

10:43.162 --> 10:46.873
Very well,
but you must promise not to speak.

10:47.207 --> 10:49.792
These old folks are a bit sensitive,
you know?

10:50.002 --> 10:52.086
Thank you, uncle.

10:58.344 --> 11:01.596
The Earth Kingdom defenses
are concentrated here,

11:01.680 --> 11:04.307
a dangerous battalion
of their strongest earthbenders,

11:04.391 --> 11:06.184
and fiercest warriors.

11:06.518 --> 11:09.604
So, I am recommending
the 41st division.

11:09.813 --> 11:12.523
But the 41st is entirely new recruits.

11:12.733 --> 11:16.319
How do you expect them to defeat
a powerful Earth Kingdom battalion?

11:16.528 --> 11:18.571
I don't.

11:18.781 --> 11:20.323
They'll be used as a distraction

11:20.407 --> 11:22.325
while we mount an attack
from the rear.

11:22.785 --> 11:26.537
What better to use as bait
than fresh meat?

11:26.956 --> 11:29.290
You can't sacrifice
an entire division like that!

11:29.375 --> 11:31.501
Those soldiers love
and defend our nation.

11:31.585 --> 11:32.919
How can you betray them?

11:36.131 --> 11:37.757
Zuko was right, you see?

11:38.175 --> 11:41.135
But it was not his place to speak out.

11:41.220 --> 11:43.930
And there were dire consequences.

11:46.892 --> 11:48.977
So you were upset
that you were the Avatar?

11:49.687 --> 11:51.521
Why wouldn't you be excited about it?

11:51.689 --> 11:54.107
Well, I didn't know
how to feel about it.

11:54.692 --> 11:56.401
All I knew was that after I found out,

11:56.735 --> 11:58.277
everything began changing.

11:59.196 --> 12:00.613
Hey, not bad.

12:00.698 --> 12:01.948
You guys have been practicing.

12:02.282 --> 12:03.658
Not only that,

12:03.742 --> 12:06.661
we made up a game you can play
with the air scooters.

12:06.870 --> 12:07.954
Great!

12:12.710 --> 12:13.835
What's going on?

12:14.211 --> 12:15.670
Now that you're the Avatar,

12:15.879 --> 12:17.505
it's kind of an unfair advantage

12:17.715 --> 12:19.090
for whichever team you're on.

12:19.299 --> 12:20.591
But I'm still the same.

12:20.801 --> 12:22.635
Nothing has changed.

12:22.720 --> 12:25.263
So, what? I can't play?

12:25.472 --> 12:26.973
That's the only fair way.

12:27.182 --> 12:29.726
Okay...

12:29.810 --> 12:31.644
Sorry, Aang.

12:32.730 --> 12:35.398
Okay, now, who wants
to have Jinju on their team?

12:45.367 --> 12:48.036
Very interesting move, young one.

12:48.162 --> 12:49.787
What do you mean?

12:54.334 --> 12:56.502
Hey! Ha ha ha!

12:56.712 --> 12:59.005
Ha ha ha!

12:59.715 --> 13:01.049
You're playing games with him?

13:01.216 --> 13:03.384
The Avatar should be training.

13:03.594 --> 13:06.179
Aang has already
trained enough for today.

13:06.388 --> 13:08.514
Time is short. Come with me.

13:08.599 --> 13:11.392
I must test you
on some high-level techniques.

13:11.810 --> 13:14.228
No. As long as I am his guardian,

13:14.313 --> 13:16.314
I will decide when he trains

13:16.607 --> 13:19.192
And when he gets his butt kicked
at Pai Sho.

13:19.610 --> 13:20.860
Hmmph!

13:26.909 --> 13:30.203
After Zuko's outburst in the meeting,

13:30.287 --> 13:33.873
the Fire Lord became
very angry with him.

13:34.875 --> 13:38.086
He said that Prince Zuko's
challenge of the general

13:38.295 --> 13:42.215
was an act of complete disrespect.

13:42.424 --> 13:45.802
And there was only one way
to resolve this.

13:45.886 --> 13:48.596
Agni Kai. A fire duel.

13:48.931 --> 13:50.681
That's right.

13:50.766 --> 13:54.018
Zuko looked upon
the old general he had insulted,

13:54.103 --> 13:56.771
and declared that he was not afraid.

13:57.231 --> 13:59.774
But Zuko misunderstood.

13:59.983 --> 14:02.276
When he turned to face his opponent,

14:02.486 --> 14:05.613
he was surprised to see
it was not the general.

14:05.906 --> 14:09.742
Zuko had spoken out
against the general's plan,

14:09.827 --> 14:12.829
but by doing so
in the Fire Lord's war room,

14:13.038 --> 14:16.958
it was the Fire Lord
whom he had disrespected.

14:17.626 --> 14:22.421
Zuko would have to duel
his own father.

14:24.133 --> 14:26.676
Then, just when
I was starting to feel better,

14:26.760 --> 14:28.553
something worse happened.

14:28.720 --> 14:31.222
Aang needs to have freedom and fun.

14:31.431 --> 14:34.642
He needs to grow up as a normal boy.

14:34.810 --> 14:38.104
You cannot keep protecting him
from his destiny.

14:38.522 --> 14:41.023
Gyatso, I know you mean well,

14:41.233 --> 14:44.819
but you are letting your affection
for the boy cloud your judgment.

14:44.903 --> 14:48.489
All I want is what is best for him.

14:48.699 --> 14:51.826
But what we need
is what's best for the world.

14:54.621 --> 14:57.832
You and Aang must be separated.

14:57.916 --> 15:00.751
The Avatar will be sent away
to the Eastern Air Temple

15:00.961 --> 15:02.712
to complete his training.

15:13.473 --> 15:14.932
That's awful, Aang.

15:15.517 --> 15:17.351
I don't know what to say.

15:17.436 --> 15:19.061
How could they do that to me?

15:19.146 --> 15:20.688
They wanted to take away
everything I knew,

15:20.772 --> 15:22.023
and everyone I loved!

15:22.232 --> 15:24.150
Whoa! Hot cinders.

15:25.485 --> 15:27.320
I'm sorry I got so mad.

15:27.863 --> 15:29.238
You have a right to be angry

15:29.323 --> 15:30.781
after the monks
sent you away like that.

15:31.241 --> 15:33.868
Well, that's not exactly
what happened.

15:39.082 --> 15:41.250
I was afraid and confused.

15:41.460 --> 15:43.294
I didn't know what to do.

15:49.301 --> 15:51.177
Aang?

15:51.261 --> 15:53.763
I'm not going to let them
take you away from me.

15:53.972 --> 15:55.139
Aang?

16:03.357 --> 16:05.650
I never saw Gyatso again.

16:21.375 --> 16:23.542
Next thing I knew,
I was waking up in your arms

16:23.627 --> 16:25.753
after you found me in the iceberg.

16:29.091 --> 16:30.216
You ran away.

16:30.592 --> 16:33.052
And then the Fire Nation
attacked our temple.

16:33.136 --> 16:35.221
My people needed me,
and I wasn't there to help.

16:35.597 --> 16:36.973
You don't know what would have--

16:37.057 --> 16:38.808
The world needed me,
and I wasn't there to help.

16:39.142 --> 16:41.018
-Aang...
-The fisherman was right.

16:41.311 --> 16:42.895
I did turn my back on the world.

16:43.355 --> 16:45.398
You're being too hard on yourself.

16:45.482 --> 16:46.857
Even if you did run away,

16:47.192 --> 16:49.026
I think it was meant to be.

16:49.403 --> 16:50.987
If you had stayed,
you would have been killed

16:51.071 --> 16:52.780
along with all the other airbenders.

16:53.031 --> 16:54.407
You don't know that.

16:54.491 --> 16:56.534
I know it's meant to be this way.

16:56.994 --> 16:59.954
The world needs you now.

17:00.038 --> 17:01.289
You give people hope.

17:07.587 --> 17:10.339
When Prince Zuko saw
that it was his father

17:10.424 --> 17:12.383
who had come to duel him,

17:12.509 --> 17:14.051
he begged for mercy.

17:15.971 --> 17:17.263
Please, father,

17:17.347 --> 17:19.348
I only had the Fire Nation's
best interests at heart.

17:19.558 --> 17:20.933
I'm sorry I spoke out of turn.

17:21.435 --> 17:24.186
You will fight for your honor.

17:24.730 --> 17:26.522
I meant you no disrespect.

17:26.606 --> 17:27.857
I am your loyal son.

17:28.191 --> 17:31.360
Rise and fight, Prince Zuko.

17:31.445 --> 17:33.112
I won't fight you.

17:33.363 --> 17:35.656
You will learn respect,

17:36.158 --> 17:39.618
and suffering will be your teacher.

17:41.538 --> 17:43.706
I looked away.

17:48.795 --> 17:52.965
I always thought that Prince Zuko
was in a training accident.

17:53.133 --> 17:55.760
It was no accident.

17:56.136 --> 17:57.762
After the duel,

17:57.846 --> 18:01.349
the Fire Lord said
that by refusing to fight,

18:02.059 --> 18:04.977
Zuko had shown shameful weakness.

18:05.395 --> 18:07.646
As punishment, he was banished,

18:07.731 --> 18:10.816
and sent to capture the Avatar.

18:11.234 --> 18:14.904
Only then could he return
with his honor.

18:15.280 --> 18:18.032
So that's why he's so obsessed.

18:18.325 --> 18:20.743
Capturing the Avatar
is the only chance he has

18:20.827 --> 18:23.079
of things returning to normal.

18:23.246 --> 18:25.331
Things will never return to normal,

18:25.499 --> 18:27.958
but the important thing is,

18:28.168 --> 18:30.544
the Avatar gives Zuko hope.

18:47.396 --> 18:50.106
Help! Please, help!

18:50.482 --> 18:52.483
It's okay. You're safe.

18:52.567 --> 18:54.360
But my husband isn't.

18:54.444 --> 18:56.612
What do you mean? Where's Sokka?

18:56.863 --> 18:58.280
They haven't returned.

18:58.365 --> 18:59.907
They should have been back by now.

19:00.033 --> 19:02.243
And this storm is becoming a typhoon.

19:02.494 --> 19:04.078
They're caught out at sea!

19:04.371 --> 19:05.704
I'm going to find them.

19:05.914 --> 19:06.956
I'm going with you.

19:07.165 --> 19:08.249
I'm staying here.

19:11.128 --> 19:13.587
We'll be back soon. I promise.

19:20.220 --> 19:21.387
Where were we hit?

19:21.471 --> 19:22.471
I don't know.

19:22.556 --> 19:24.390
Look!

19:24.975 --> 19:26.267
The helmsman!

19:43.160 --> 19:44.326
Aah!

19:54.463 --> 19:55.796
Where are they?

19:58.925 --> 20:00.926
Come on, Appa!

20:11.897 --> 20:13.689
The boat! There!

20:16.318 --> 20:17.693
The Avatar!

20:17.777 --> 20:20.362
What do you want to do, sir?

20:20.447 --> 20:21.989
Let him go.

20:22.073 --> 20:23.991
We need to get this ship to safety.

20:24.201 --> 20:28.078
Then we must head directly
into the eye of the storm.

20:36.880 --> 20:38.631
I'm too young to die!

20:38.715 --> 20:40.508
I'm not, but I still don't want to!

20:55.774 --> 20:57.024
Hang on to the rope!

21:01.446 --> 21:02.988
Whoa! Whoa!

21:50.036 --> 21:52.413
Uncle, I am sorry.

21:52.831 --> 21:54.915
Your apology is accepted.

22:15.729 --> 22:17.813
You're alive!

22:18.440 --> 22:20.357
You owe this boy an apology.

22:20.442 --> 22:22.276
He doesn't have to apologize.

22:22.360 --> 22:25.154
What if, instead of an apology,

22:25.238 --> 22:27.656
I give him a free fish,
and we call it even?

22:27.866 --> 22:29.617
Actually, I don't eat meat.

22:29.743 --> 22:31.076
Fish ain't meat.

22:31.494 --> 22:33.621
Seriously, you're still gonna pay me,
right?

22:34.914 --> 22:35.914
Aah!

22:36.166 --> 22:38.042
Katara, I think you were right before.

22:38.293 --> 22:39.585
I'm done dwelling on the past.

22:39.669 --> 22:40.794
Really?

22:41.004 --> 22:43.047
I can't make guesses about
how things would have turned out

22:43.131 --> 22:44.340
If I hadn't run away.

22:45.050 --> 22:46.967
I'm here now, and I'm going
to make the most of it.

22:47.344 --> 22:49.637
I don't think you're gonna have
those nightmares anymore.

22:50.639 --> 22:52.431
If you weren't here now...

22:52.557 --> 22:54.975
Well, I guess, I wouldn't be either.

22:55.185 --> 22:57.728
Thank you for saving my life, Avatar.

22:59.564 --> 23:01.357
Do you hear that?

23:01.441 --> 23:02.441
It stopped raining.

23:09.741 --> 23:11.867
Appa!
